        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "aac65bc5-425c-5091-8d8b-1fa0ccd8747b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marcia Wallace, Edna Krabappel, David Silverman, Lance Kramer, Dan Castellaneta, Julie Kavner, Nancy Cartwright, Yeardley Smith, Hank Azaria, Harry Shearer, Tress MacNeille, Pamela Hayden, Maggie Roswell, Russi Taylor, Tom Hanks, Albert Brooks\n- Works: The Bob Newhart Show, The Simpsons, The Simpsons Movie\n- Roles: Carol Kester, Edna Krabappel, Bart Simpson's 4th grade teacher, Ned Flanders's wife, director, additional sequence director\n- Organizations/Places: Springfield Elementary School\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1970s, Marcia Wallace played receptionist Carol Kester on the sitcom \"The Bob Newhart Show\".\n- In 1992, Marcia Wallace won an Emmy for voicing Edna Krabappel on the animated series \"The Simpsons\".\n- Edna Krabappel is Bart Simpson's 4th grade teacher at Springfield Elementary School in \"The Simpsons\".\n- In later seasons of \"The Simpsons\", Edna Krabappel becomes Ned Flanders's wife.\n- Marcia Wallace is also known for voicing Edna Krabappel on \"The Simpsons\".\n- \"The Simpsons Movie\" was directed by David Silverman.\n- Lance Kramer served as an additional sequence director for \"The Simpsons Movie\".\n- \"The Simpsons Movie\" stars the regular television cast of Dan Castellaneta, Julie Kavner, Nancy Cartwright, Yeardley Smith, Hank Azaria, Harry Shearer, Tress MacNeille, Pamela Hayden, Marcia Wallace, Maggie Roswell, and Russi Taylor, along with Tom Hanks, Green Day, and Albert Brooks.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
